 "comments": [
  {
   "rating": 41,
   "date": "2006-06-13T14:17:01-05:00",
   "body": "Starting location:\nNext to the lighthouse Southern Westfall coastline (30.86)\n\nOracles:\nRight at the coast near the lighthouse (33.83)\n\nWarriors:\nHead North along the coast after taking out Oracles and you will encounter the Warriors. (36.22)\n\nCoastrunners:\nAfter Warriors keep going North and you will finally find the Coastrunners. (54.10)",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 31,
   "date": "2005-10-01T02:17:01-05:00",
   "body": "When you get the quest, the Oracles and the Tidehunters are nearby. The other two (Coast Runner & Warrior) are a little more elusive.\n\nGo North up the coast and you will eventually run into the Warriors. (level 14-15) Kill 7, and keep going!&nbsp; All the way up towards the North-most part of the coast you'll finally find the Coast Runners.&nbsp; They're level 11-12.\n\nWhy do they send someone on a level 19 quest to kill level 11's?&nbsp; I don't know... But it's worth about 1450exp at level 19.",
   "replies": [
    "Thank you for putting in the location of the other beasts...I couldn't find them!&nbsp; Best Wishes, Charr"
   ]
  },
  {
   "rating": 16,
   "date": "2006-08-25T14:17:01-05:00",
   "body": "Once you get this quest, head up North to the [b]very top[/b] of the coast, North of the pumpkin farm.&nbsp; Coastrunners are up there.\n\nThen just work your way down the beach; you'll run into Warriors, then Oracles, & finally Tidehunters.\n\nAnd then you can turn in at the Lighthouse.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 13,
   "date": "2007-03-25T10:53:06-05:00",
   "body": "The Horde can do this quest",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 7,
   "date": "2006-10-01T02:17:01-05:00",
   "body": "When you're going down there its a good idea to bring at least one friend whether they have the quest or not, I have died alot because the stupid Murlocs net me and run off towards the camp and bring back like 10 others they net me and then slaughter me with a combo of DoT poisons and High DPS, whcih sucks because if I wasn't netted I'd be sprinting out of there. So bring a friend, prefferably one with ranged attack like a Hunter or Mage/Lock/Priest.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 6,
   "date": "2007-04-01T14:17:01-05:00",
   "body": "I'm sure that is being confused with the infamous Westfall Stew quest.&nbsp; A lvl 10 would never make it to the Lighthouse where it is picked up.\n\nI picked it up at lvl 20 being sent down from SW on the pally quest next to the DM exit.&nbsp; \n\nThe Tidewater and Orcales, typical Merloc kills, intresting that I actually killed the lvl 20 big murloc yet it was walking further up the coast being in two places at once.&nbsp; The warriors were much more north, mixing in the hunter made it worth chasing lvl 15-16\n\nHaving to go back to lvl 12-13 murlocs to finish a lvl 19 quest is insane espically since it is literally on the other side of westfall and I will have to return to turn in at the Lighthouse.&nbsp; Disappointing.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2005-02-12T11:59:32-06:00",
   "body": "Acutally, XP gained is based on your level when you turn the quest in, the lower your level, the more you will get.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2005-03-06T06:11:56-06:00",
   "body": "this quest is horde and alliance  i did it with my tauren hunter",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 0,
   "date": "2006-01-18T14:17:01-06:00",
   "body": "Nevermind...I found him.&nbsp; Someone actually led me to him.&nbsp; If anyone else can't find him, he's outside the Westfall Lighthouse which is on a little island a little ways past Moonbrook.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 0,
